+empty-apply stub that only declares the config row.
+
+Documented surface, as this fixture states it:
+
+- **Toolview takeover.** One registration per grouped tool into the keyed
+  `tool.call.toolview` slot at `priority: -1`, so the plugin's row renders
+  instead of the shipped `read`/`grep`/`glob` rows. `tools: []` covers the
+  three built-ins; a non-empty list is an explicit wire-name whitelist.
+- **Run merge.** Consecutive same-tool calls in the chat flow become one card:
+  the group head renders a count summary plus one compact child row per call,
+  every other seat renders nothing. `groupBy: adjacent` merges any consecutive
+  run; `groupBy: step` restricts the run to one agent step; `maxGroupSize`
+  caps a group and starts a new one for the excess (no call is dropped).
+- **Per-call card material.** The merged card re-derives the shipped read and
+  terminal card inputs from raw block fields (`argsRaw`, `content`, `meta`).
+- **Localized row copy.** The plugin's own `zh`/`en` dictionaries register
+  into the `locale` service; the optional `betterLocale` service (probed with
+  `ctx.get`, no runtime dependency) receives the per-language override dicts
+  and is re-synced on every locale revision.
+- **Config row.** `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the `bench-merge-calls` row with
+  `tools`/`groupBy`/`maxGroupSize`; the host half declares the validated shape.
+- **Style seam.** A `[data-chat-flow-kind="tool-call"]:has([data-slot="tool.call.toolview"]:empty)`
+  rule collapses the empty continuation seats from the chat flow (best-effort:
+  a browser without `:has()` only keeps flow spacing).
+
+Cohort: migrated to the **0.1.2-alpha.2** host line. The browser half reads the
+chat snapshot through ui-chat's `useChat` session hook, takes owner data from
+`ToolCallOwnerProps`, and derives cards from raw call/result fields — the
+0.1.1-era `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` type surface, its session-store
+chat slice, and the `resultView`/`callView` call-object fields are gone.
+
+Required harness patch: `patches/0001-carry-client-row-config-to-the-browser-half.patch`
+(the `dsh.client` browser half receives its Loader row's config). The merged
+card renders without it; only the row knobs are inert.
 
